From: Stephen Kent <43362477+kentstephen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:45:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ranges=: accept ISO date bounds via CF time units

A bound that is not a number is resolved at bind against the coordinate's
CF `units` attribute (`<unit> since <epoch>`; seconds/minutes/hours/days,
standard/gregorian/proleptic_gregorian calendars) into the coordinate's own
raw values, so `time:2020-07-01:2020-07-01T23` works on ERA5 without the
user computing hours since 1959. Bounds are parsed as text (DimRangeSpec)
and resolved once coordinates are loaded. The lo:hi separator is found by
choosing the colon at which both sides are well-formed tokens, since ISO
times contain colons. No new dependencies: civil-date arithmetic is inline.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015DQGNDQN7rRXCfEQ7wL4cr
